  sedentary minutes. 2005_2006 has no GPAQ items and is excluded from this arm
  rather than imputed; base and arm are refit on the same 2007+ women.
  I: physical activity (MET + sedentary) n   932  events  550  base 0.754 -> arm 0.757  delta +0.004 [-0.002, +0.009]  no detectable gain
  Arm I2 — the specialist's secondary activity measures: moderate and vigorous
  minutes per week (log scale) plus sitting time, on the same 2007+ women.
  I2: moderate + vigorous min/week + sitting n   932  events  550  base 0.754 -> arm 0.757  delta +0.003 [-0.002, +0.009]  no detectable gain

  Arm J — sleep in the specialist's five bands (<=5, 6, 7-8 ref, 9, >=10 h).
  A SUBSTITUTION for continuous sleep hours, never an addition.
  J: sleep in five bands (substitution) n 1,107  events  643  base 0.750 -> arm 0.749  delta -0.001 [-0.007, +0.006]  no detectable gain

  Arm G — diabetes. The diabetic bone paradox means type 2 diabetes raises
  measured BMD while also raising fracture risk, so a protective coefficient
  here is expected and is NOT evidence the model is wrong. There is
  deliberately no EXPECTED_SIGNS entry for it. Two reclassifications:
    G1: borderline coded as diabetic       AUC 0.755  (shipped 0.755, delta +0.001)
    G2: diabetes dropped entirely          AUC 0.755  (shipped 0.755, delta -0.000)

  Arm H — site sensitivity. The headline uses the WHO/ISCD lowest-of-two
  rule. These refit on each site alone to show the rule is not driving the
  result. Reported for the headline target only, and never re-ablated.
    H1: femoral neck only      n 1,111  events  618  AUC 0.747  (Ridge -> t_score)
    H2: total hip only         n 1,111  events  424  AUC 0.776  (Ridge -> t_score)
